tags: descendant-accounts

A limit of the node: the most accounts of descendants below one account.

The value is an integer in accounts. Example: 200. The node refuses a start that makes more descendants.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=descendant-accounts
per=one account
rule=The node refuses a start that makes more descendants.
scope=none
unit=accounts
